<Site title="About" description="Our mission, our vision, and who PictureThis Production is for: free live-production training for communities the industry rarely reaches.">
  <section>
    <h1>About PictureThis Production</h1>
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>PictureThis Production opens the door to live production careers. We offer free, hands-on training and mentorship in sound, cameras, lighting, and streaming, learned on real shows beside working technicians. Everyone who trains with us leaves with a trade, a reference, and a path into paid work.</p>
    <h2>Vision</h2>
    <p>A Toronto where young people build their future together, not on the streets, but as a crew: learning skills, earning a living, and looking out for one another.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="who-this-is-for">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Our cohorts are built for people the industry rarely reaches: young people ages 16 to 29 from under-resourced neighbourhoods, people rebuilding after the justice system or in recovery, women, families, and people with disabilities, with outreach in Black, Ghanaian, and French-speaking communities.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Young people, 16 to 29.</strong> Our cohort program: eight weeks of free training on real shows. Applications are open for January.</li>
      <li><strong>People rebuilding.</strong> If you are coming out of the justice system and rebuilding, there is a place for you on a crew: a trade, a mentor, and a fresh reference.</li>
      <li><strong>People in recovery.</strong> Structured training, a sober crew, and a path to paid work while you get your life back.</li>
      <li><strong>Women.</strong> Technical production is still mostly men. We are making room, on purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Children and families.</strong> Age-appropriate production experiences for children, always with a parent or guardian present.</li>
      <li><strong>People with disabilities.</strong> Training, roles, and venues adapted so you can actually do the work, not just watch it.</li>
      <li><strong>Our communities.</strong> We do outreach in Black, Ghanaian, and French-speaking communities, in the places people already gather.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>One cohort, every community. The January cohort is open to anyone on this list. If you see yourself here, apply.</p>
  </section>
</Site>

